    <heading level="1">Section 2.1 Exercises</heading>
    <heading level="1">Practice Makes Perfect</heading>
    <paragraph>Solve Equations Using the General Strategy</paragraph>
    <paragraph>In the following exercises, determine whether the given values are solutions to the equation.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="1" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$6y + 10 = 12y$$</paragraph>
        <paragraph>ⓐ $$y = \frac{5}{3}$$ ⓑ $$y = - \frac{1}{2}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>ⓐ yes ⓑ no</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="2" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$4x + 9 = 8x$$</paragraph>
        <paragraph>ⓐ $$x = - \frac{7}{8}$$ ⓑ $$x = \frac{9}{4}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
